{
  "title": "GPCR-DMS Database: raw per-variant GPCR mutational scanning data by study, aligned to GPCRdb numbering",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "upload_type": "dataset",
  "description": "<p>Per-variant measurements from 21 published GPCR studies (deep mutational scans, receptor-wide alanine scans and variant panels) across 14 human receptors, in 24 datasets (one folder per receptor per study). Each study keeps its original files unmodified (<code>source/</code>) plus every per-variant table as CSV (<code>tables/</code>) with all of the authors' columns, and every table additionally carries GPCRdb generic and Ballesteros-Weinstein residue numbers so positions can be compared across receptors. A merged long table (<code>merged/</code>) puts every study's main published score in one file, one row per variant per condition, with optional rescaled scores for comparing conditions. Every derived file is rebuilt from <code>source/</code> by <code>code/build.py</code>.</p><p><strong>Licensing:</strong> every dataset was published by someone else and keeps its own license; there is no single license over the collection. The MIT license applies only to the compilation (scripts, column layout, GPCRdb join, documentation). Four datasets are non-commercial (RHO_Chen2026 and CNR2_MoralesPastor2025 CC BY-NC-ND 4.0; AGTR1_Boora2026 and PTGFR_Boora2026 CC BY-NC 4.0) and AGTR1_Cao2023 carries no stated reuse license. See LICENSE.md, NOTICE.md and each study's LICENSE.txt. Please cite the original paper for each dataset you use (REFERENCES.md), and GPCRdb.</p>",
  "creators": [
    {
      "name": "Howard, Matthew K.",
      "affiliation": "University of California, San Francisco"
    }
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "access_right": "open",
  "keywords": [
    "GPCR",
    "deep mutational scanning",
    "alanine scanning",
    "GPCRdb",
    "variant effect",
    "MaveDB"
  ],
